![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The use of `shift 2` without verifying that a value follows the option flag can cause the script to exit unexpectedly under `set -e` if the user provides a trailing flag without a value (e.g., `aidevops plugin add <url> --namespace`). Consider validating that `$#` is greater than 1 before shifting.

```suggestion
		case "$_opt" in
		--namespace | --ns)
			[[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { print_error "Value required for $_opt"; return 1; }
			namespace="$_val"
			shift 2
			;;
		--branch | -b)
			[[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { print_error "Value required for $_opt"; return 1; }
			branch="$_val"
			shift 2
			;;
		--name | -n)
			[[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { print_error "Value required for $_opt"; return 1; }
			plugin_name="$_val"
			shift 2
			;;
```

