![security-critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/security-critical.svg) ![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

Using `execSync` with a shell string constructed from `JSON.stringify(filePath)` is vulnerable to command injection in Bash. While `JSON.stringify` escapes double quotes, it does not escape shell-special characters like `$` or backticks (`` ` ``), which Bash will evaluate even inside double quotes. Since `shell: "/bin/bash"` is explicitly used, this is a critical security risk. Use `execFileSync` to pass arguments as an array, bypassing the shell entirely.

```javascript
      const sig = execFileSync(helperPath, ["footer", "--body", current], {
        encoding: "utf-8",
        timeout: 5000,
        stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe"],
      });
```

