![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The comment incorrectly states that checkSignatureFooterGate is called in handleToolAfter. It is actually invoked within handleToolBefore (line 251).

```suggestion
// re-export only and does NOT create a local binding - checkSignatureFooterGate 
// is called locally at handleToolBefore below, so it must be imported into
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The parseNames function does not correctly handle import aliases. For a statement like import { X as Y }, the local binding is Y, but this function currently returns X. This will lead to false positives where a correctly imported identifier is flagged as a violation if it is also re-exported.

```javascript
function parseNames(block, isImport = false) {
  return block
    .split(",")
    .map((s) => {
      const parts = s.trim().split(/\s+as\s+/);
      return (isImport && parts.length > 1 ? parts[1] : parts[0]).trim();
    })
    .filter(Boolean);
}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The regexes for reExportRe and importRe use the $ anchor without accounting for potential trailing comments. This can cause the regex to fail on valid statements (e.g., import { X } from "./Y"; // comment), which results in the identifiers inside those blocks being incorrectly flagged as local uses.

```suggestion
  const reExportRe = /^export\s*\{([^}]+)\}\s*from\s*["'][^"']+["'];?\s*(?:\/\/.*)?$/gm;
  const importRe = /^import\s*\{([^}]+)\}\s*from\s*["'][^"']+["'];?\s*(?:\/\/.*)?$/gm;
```

